            <ArticleTitle>Ductal Adenocarcinoma of the Prostate: A Case Report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>802-805</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1159/000453448</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Ductal adenocarcinoma is an unusual variant of adenocarcinoma of the prostate. A 73-year-old male was referred to our hospital for the further examination of an elevated prostate-specific antigen level of 23.4 ng/mL. Radical prostatectomy (RP) was performed based on the diagnosis obtained by a prostate needle biopsy. The RP specimen revealed ductal adenocarcinoma of the prostate with positive capsular penetration. We herein report a rare case of ductal adenocarcinoma of the prostate.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
